# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution; 1 rad = 1.59 mm). hv0.sim_dist, zeroed at the failure, is how
# far the axis went.
# The dynamic brake can't hold the current: its target here is 0.45 A
# (dbrake0.max_cur 0.5), the short alone draws ~2 A, more than 1.3 x the
# target for 2 ms. It gives up rather than overload the power stage: the
# outputs go off and the axis coasts (~16 rad).
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
dbrake0.max_cur = 0.5
hv0.sim_dist = 0
enc_fb0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.003
fault0.stop
run 0.006
fault0.stop
fault0.en_out
run 0.4
hv0.sim_dist
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 2
@expect fault0.stop[2] == 0
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
@expect hv0.sim_dist > 12
